    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p46_b11",
      "text": "Training architecture and run management.\nThe training system is built on\nVERL/HybridFlow [Sheng et al., 2024] with Ray orchestration [Moritz et al., 2018] and\nvLLM rollout [Kwon et al., 2023]. Each run has a Ray task runner that builds the\nprompt datasets, initializes the actor/rollout/reference worker group, and launches the\nreward-scoring manager. The actor is the only trainable policy model in GRPO-style\nruns. A frozen reference copy of the initial policy is kept for log-probability and KL\ndiagnostics; it is not optimized. For PPO runs, we additionally enable the critic/value\nmodel and use GAE. Rollouts are generated by vLLM in asynchronous mode, while\nold-policy and reference log probabilities are recomputed by the VERL workers before\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.57,
        466.49,
        523.68,
        622.0
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
